{
  "info": {
    "name": "Tri9T AI — CT-200 (versioning + staleness demo)",
    "_postman_id": "b8f3c2e1-4a5d-4f6e-9c7b-1d2e3f4a5b6c",
    "description": "End-to-end demo of the Tri9T AI backend. Covers ingestion verification, browse, version-pinned selections, LLM generation, and staleness detection.\n\n**Prerequisites:**\n- Server running at http://localhost:8000\n- Both v1 and v2 PDFs ingested (run `python -m scripts.ingest_cli data/raw/ct200_manual.pdf \"CardioTrack CT-200\"` and the v2 equivalent)\n- Valid GROQ_API_KEY in .env\n\n**How to run:**\n1. Import this collection\n2. Click \"Run\" (top-right of the collection)\n3. All 5 folders execute in order, setting variables between requests\n4. Green checkmarks = everything working; the last step proves the staleness distinction\n\n**Key demonstration:**\n- Battery Life (v1: 300 cycles → v2: 250 cycles) → `stale / critical / numeric_threshold_changed`\n- Overpressure Protection (identical in v1 and v2) → `fresh / none / unchanged`",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Setup & health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('API is up', () => {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('ok');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/health", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["health"] }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "LLM config (verify key + model)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('LLM is configured', () => {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(j.provider).to.eql('groq');",
                  "    pm.expect(j.groq_key_is_gsk).to.be.true;",
                  "    pm.expect(j.groq_key_length).to.be.above(40);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/debug/llm-config", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["debug", "llm-config"] }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
